  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222799_PAPUA NEW GUINEA - START FUND- ENGA LANDSLIDE RESPONSE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The agency aims to address the immediate life-saving needs of communities affected by a devastating landslide. With a focus on vulnerable populations, the project plans to support approximately 1,963 impacted individuals (approximately 393 households), prioritizing those residing in Temporary Care Centers. Priority will be given to households with children under five, child-headed households, female-headed households, the elderly, people with disabilities, pregnant and lactating women. Protection measures will be integrated, and activities will include providing safe water, sanitation, and hygiene promotion. Additionally, the project will facilitate rehabilitation of water supply systems, emergency latrines, water trucking, distribution of shelter materials, and dissemination of protection messaging. Furthermore, the project aims to conduct Disaster Risk Reduction assessments and workshops to help communities prepare for and respond to future disasters.</narrative>
  </description>
